# This business's settings. In Vercel: the project's Settings → Environment
# Variables (Production — and Preview only if previews should run real jobs).
# "Set up on Vercel" in Scallle fills in the first two for you.
# Locally: copy to .env.local. Never commit real values.
#
# There is no secret to set: Scallle signs every job with its own key and this
# project checks it against the keys Scallle publishes at SCALLLE_APP_URL.

# This business's workspace id in Scallle (a UUID). Jobs for any other
# workspace are refused, and nothing runs until this is a UUID. The step in
# Scallle shows it under the code project's settings once the project's
# address is connected there (connecting sends nothing).
SCALLLE_WORKSPACE_ID=

# Where Scallle lives. Scallle's public job keys are fetched only from here,
# and results are only ever posted back here.
SCALLLE_APP_URL=https://app.scallle.com

# Optional. The business's OWN Anthropic API key — ideally from an Anthropic
# workspace just for this business, so its spend and data settings sit apart.
# Leave it unset to call Claude through Vercel AI Gateway on the business's
# Vercel account instead (needs AI Gateway credit and a Pro plan; see README).
# After adding or changing it in Vercel, redeploy.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Local development only (see README → Local development) ---
# Point Claude calls at the mock instead of Anthropic or AI Gateway (no key,
# no cost). NEVER set this in Vercel: unless SCALLLE_APP_URL is local too,
# every job is refused while it is set.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4020
